{#- A place's section chips (docs/features/navigation README §4.9, D6, D8; COM-02, PUZ-01; decision 75): rendered by
    base.html.twig's section_chips block at the top of <main> on every page nav_section_chips() gives a row for -
    Community: Leaderboards · Puzzlers · Events on every page of those sections (the leaderboards' own pill row stays
    under it: two levels); Puzzles: My library (signed-in) · All puzzles · Marketplace · What next? on its four start
    pages. Labels from the registry (SectionChipsBuilder), aria-current "page" on the page a chip links to, "true"
    deeper inside its section. One row, never wrapped or cut: it scrolls sideways on phones and the current chip is
    brought into view (section_chips_controller.js - the row only, never the page). data-ptr-ignore: a pull that starts
    on the row never refreshes the page. Guests' HTML: the URL decides everything, nothing per visitor.
    Not chrome (it sits in <main> and stays in the app); no heading, no form; data-nav on every link. -#}
{%- set section_chips = nav_section_chips() -%}
{%- if section_chips is not null -%}
<nav class="section-chips container px-3" aria-label="{{ section_chips.label|trans }}" data-ptr-ignore data-controller="section-chips">
    <div class="section-chips-row" data-section-chips-target="row">
    {%- for chip in section_chips.chips -%}
        <a class="section-chip" href="{{ chip.href }}" data-press data-nav="chips/{{ section_chips.place.value }}/{{ chip.section }}"
        {%- if chip.current %} aria-current="{{ chip.current }}" data-section-chips-target="active"{% endif %}
        {%- if chip.section == 'library' %} rel="nofollow"{% endif %}>{{ chip.label|trans }}</a>
    {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
</nav>
{%- endif -%}
